<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Crisis</p><h1 class="enc-title">Third Taiwan Strait Crisis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1995">1995</a>–<a href="/years/1996">1996</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Third <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan-strait">Taiwan Strait</a> Crisis was a period of military tension in 1995–1996, triggered by Taiwanese President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lee-teng-hui">Lee Teng-hui</a>'s visit to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> in June 1995. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a> fired missiles into waters near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a> and held exercises before Taiwan's first direct presidential election in March 1996. The United States sent two aircraft carrier groups to the region, and Lee won the election.</p></div>
